  "requirement": "Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the refresh token is not enough. If tokens live longer than that limit, push the revocation to each service (for example, with OpenID CAEP session-revoked events) or make the tokens shorter-lived.",
  "not_covered": [
    {
      "problem": "A kill switch that doesn't stop running work or open tool streams",
      "owner": "R11"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Sub-agents or remote workers still acting after the parent is stopped",
      "owner": "E09"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Static API keys used where short-lived credentials are available",
      "owner": "B03"
    },
    {
      "problem": "No way to trace a suspicious action to its team, operator, and live instance",
      "owner": "A05"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [],
  "violates": [
    "The agent must not need to cooperate.",
    "Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect.",
    "A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm."
  ],
  "also_affects": [],
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "B04.2",
      "check": "Revocation is applied at a trusted enforcement point (identity provider, gateway, or target service) and does not need the agent's cooperation.",
      "verify": "1) Find where revocation is checked (gateway, auth middleware, IdP, introspection, deny list lookup). 2) Check it runs outside the agent process. 3) Answer no if revocation sends a message or signal to the agent and relies on it to drop credentials, or the check runs inside agent code.",
      "met": "no",
      "evidence": "app/loop.py:127, app/killswitch.py:26, app/killswitch.py:28",
      "quote": "        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n    row = await pool.fetchrow(_QUERY, f\"tenant:{tenant}\")\n        raise AgentHalted(",
      "counter_search": "",
      "note": "[challenge] The supplied operator halt is enforced by a query and exception inside the agent process, requiring agent cooperation. Operators control the database flag, but the database does not independently block integration calls. No external revocation enforcement implementation is supplied."
    },
    {
      "id": "B04.3",
      "check": "Later calls are blocked even with cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions: token lifetime is shorter than the revocation limit, or revocation is pushed to each service (for example CAEP) or checked on every call.",
      "verify": "1) Find access-token lifetimes and how services validate tokens (signature only vs `introspect`, deny list, CAEP). 2) Compare lifetime with the stated revocation limit. 3) Answer no if self-contained JWTs outlive the limit and are checked by signature only, cached tokens or open sessions skip the check, or no limit is stated. Answer unknown if validation lives outside this repo.",
      "met": "no",
      "evidence": "app/identity.py:97, app/identity.py:98, app/identity.py:115, app/loop.py:173",
      "quote": "        if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\n            return cached.value\n        token = _CachedToken(body[\"access_token\"], time.time() + int(body[\"expires_in\"]))\n                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))",
      "counter_search": "",
      "note": "[challenge] No revocation time limit or measurement is stated anywhere in the supplied files. Cached access tokens use the STS-provided expires_in without a configured revocation bound. The halt check occurs only before the run loop, so an already-running agent can continue tool calls after the flag is set. Searches for revoke, disable, session, CAEP, introspection, expiry and lifetime found no per-call external revocation policy or session cutoff bound. The projected workload token's 600-second lifetime does not bound exchanged access tokens."
    }
  ],
  "red_flags_found": [
    "app/loop.py:127, app/killswitch.py:26, app/killswitch.py:28 The supplied operator halt is enforced by a query and exception inside the agent process, requiring agent cooperation. Operators control the database flag, but the database does not independently block integration calls. No external revocation enforcement implementation is supplied.",
    "app/identity.py:97, app/identity.py:98, app/identity.py:115, app/loop.py:173 No revocation time limit or measurement is stated anywhere in the supplied files. Cached access tokens use the STS-provided expires_in without a configured revocation bound. The halt check occurs only before the run loop, so an already-running agent can continue tool calls after the flag is set. Searches for revoke, disable, session, CAEP, introspection, expiry and lifetime found no per-call external revocation policy or session cutoff bound. The projected workload token's 600-second lifetime does not bound exchanged access tokens."
  ]
}
{
  "item": "B10",
  "requirement": "Pin the container by digest. Before it runs, check its digest and signature against an approved signing key, or an approved certificate identity and issuer. Keep its build provenance (the record of how it was built) and its list of dependencies. Check provenance fields such as the builder, source repository, build type, and the parameters set from outside the build (SLSA `externalParameters`) against what you expect. Keep the verifier patched. Cosign versions before 2.6.2 and 3.0.4 could accept a bundle whose transparency-log entry didn't match the artifact. Confirm that the admission check covers production namespaces and is set to enforce, not just audit. Show that an unapproved or changed image is rejected.",
  "not_covered": [
    {
      "problem": "Tool or MCP server package not vetted or pinned",
      "owner": "E02"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Model weights or adapters loaded without a signature or format check",
      "owner": "C05"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Image runs as root or includes a shell or package manager",
      "owner": "B11"
    },
    {
      "problem": "Secrets baked into the image",
      "owner": "B03"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml",
      "line": 32,
      "note": "Production image and Dockerfile stages pinned to digests."
    }
  ],
  "violates": [
    "denies images that match no policy"
  ],
  "also_affects": [],
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "B10.4",
      "check": "The policy is in enforce mode, covers production namespaces, and denies images that match no policy.",
      "verify": "1) Read the policy mode and scope (`validationFailureAction`, `failureAction`, `mode`, namespace selectors, exclusions). 2) Check for a no-match deny. 3) Answer no if mode is `Audit` or `warn`, production namespaces are excluded or unmatched, `failurePolicy: Ignore`, or images matching no policy are allowed.",
      "met": "no",
      "evidence": "deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:24, deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:26, deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:36",
      "quote": "            =(initContainers):\n            containers:\n            - \"registry.example-corp.test/procurement/*\"",
      "counter_search": "Checked match scopes and registry pattern; production Pods covered, required signatures and failurePolicy Fail.",
      "note": "[challenge] Although Enforce, Fail, and procurement-prod scope are configured, the only-approved-registry pattern constrains only initContainers and containers. It omits spec.ephemeralContainers. A production Pod with compliant regular containers can therefore have an ephemeral container image from an unrelated registry: that image is unconstrained by the pattern and matches none of the verifyImages imageReferences. No other admission policy in agent closes this path."
    }
  ],
  "red_flags_found": [
    "deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:24, deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:26, deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml:36 Although Enforce, Fail, and procurement-prod scope are configured, the only-approved-registry pattern constrains only initContainers and containers. It omits spec.ephemeralContainers. A production Pod with compliant regular containers can therefore have an ephemeral container image from an unrelated registry: that image is unconstrained by the pattern and matches none of the verifyImages imageReferences. No other admission policy in agent closes this path."
  ]
}
