es across servers","owner":"E05"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"config/tools.yaml","line":4,"note":"Both configured roles have named tool inventories with task reasons."}],"checks":[{"id":"B01.1","check":"Each agent role has one explicit allowlist of tool names, with no wildcard grants such as `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, or `bypassPermissions`.","verify":"1) Find where each agent is built and tools are passed (`allowed_tools`, `tools=[`, `allowedTools`, `.mcp.json`, `settings.json`). 2) Check each role has one fixed list of names. 3) Answer no if any list holds `*`, `mcp__*`, `Bash(*)`, a pattern or regex, `bypassPermissions`, or is built from `list_tools()`, or if a second agent role or entry point has no list.","met":"no","evidence":"app/extractor.py:25","quote":"EXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"","counter_search":"","note":"Runtime extractor role lacks matching configured list; registry defaults to procurement rather than rejecting unmapped role."},{"id":"B01.2","check":"Tools discovered from MCP servers are filtered against that allowlist before the model can see or call them.","verify":"1) Find MCP discovery (`list_tools`, `session.list_tools`, `tools/list`, MCP client setup). 2) Trace the result to where it is handed to the model. 3) Confirm a filter keeps only names on the allowlist. 4) Answer no if any discovered tool reaches the model unfiltered, the filter is a denylist or prefix match (`startswith`, `mcp__server__`), or a refresh or reconnect path skips it.","met":"no","evidence":"app/mcp_client.py:110","quote":"self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}","counter_search":"","note":"Refresh bypasses pinned operation filtering; generic erp_call reaches newly discovered operations."},{"id":"B01.3","check":"The dispatcher rejects a call to any tool name not on the allowlist, instead of looking it up dynamically.","verify":"1) Find the dispatcher (search `tool_use`, `call_tool`, `dispatch`, `execute`, `getattr`, `registry[