r normal logs","owner":"R03"},{"problem":"Container image not pinned by digest or signature-checked","owner":"B10"}],"rating":"needs_evidence","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/identity.py","line":104,"note":"Integrations exchange runtime projected workload identity through STS."}],"checks":[{"id":"B03.1","check":"Credentials are fetched at run time from a managed identity or secrets service, not fixed API keys, where short-lived or federated credentials are available.","verify":"1) Find credential setup (`AssumeRole`, IRSA, Workload Identity, Managed Identity, Vault, `os.environ`, `process.env`). 2) Check each credential is fetched at run time. 3) Answer no if a fixed key (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `API_KEY` in a Secret or env) is used for a service that offers federated or short-lived credentials, or code falls back to a static key when the managed source fails.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"[challenge: unclear] ERP, payments and Slack-proxy credentials are exchanged at runtime from the projected workload token, with no static-key fallback. The model client supplies no explicit credential source; its external credential provisioning and availability of federated credentials cannot be established from this repository. Mounted signing keys likewise have no provisioning policy here."},{"id":"B03.2","check":"Credential lifetime and rotation are set in config to bounded values.","verify":"1) Search for lifetime and rotation settings (`DurationSeconds`, `ttl`, `expires_in`, `max_ttl`, rotation job or policy). 2) Check each credential the agent uses has a bounded value. 3) Answer no if any credential has no expiry, no rotation, or an unbounded or very long value. Answer unknown if lifetimes are set in an identity provider outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"[challenge: unclear] The workload token has a bounded 600-second lifetime and cached exchanged tokens are refreshed before their reported expiry. The STS determines expires_in externally, with no local maximum; model credentials and mounted signing-key expiry/rotation policies are also absent. These omissions do not prove the external policies are unbounded. No lifetime rationale is supplied."},{"id":"B03.3","check":"No long-lived secrets appear in prompts, Dockerfiles or image layers, or checked-in config.","verify":"1) Search prompt templates, Dockerfiles (`ENV`, `ARG`, `COPY .env`), `.env*`, `*.yaml`, `*.tfvars`, `.mcp.json` `env` blocks for key-like literals (`sk-`, `AKIA`, `token:`, `password:`). 2) Check prompt-building code for env values inserted into messages. 3) Answer no if any real secret is checked in, baked into an image, or placed in a prompt; `.gitignore` listing a file does not count if it is committed.","met":"yes","evidence":"Dockerfile:19","quote":"COPY release/manifest.yaml /app/release/manifest.yaml","counter_search":"Searched key-like values and prompt construction; secret paths only, no values inserted into prompts or image.","note":"Inspected prompts, checked-in config and final image copies; no secret literals found."},{"id":"B03.4","check":"Where the service supports it, tokens are bound to their holder with mTLS, DPoP, or workload proof tokens.","verify":"1) Find token and client setup for each service (`mTLS`, `client_cert`, `DPoP`, `cert-bound`, SPIFFE). 2) Check whether the service supports holder binding. 3) Answer no if a supporting service uses plain bearer tokens. Answer unknown if support depends on a provider outside this repo and nothing states it.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"[challenge: unclear] Integration clients send bearer tokens without visible mTLS client certificates, DPoP or per-request workload proofs. Exchanging a workload token and restricting audience does not itself establish holder binding. The repository does not specify whether the external STS and target services support such binding