digest compare and a signature check run before use. 3) Answer no if either is missing, wrapped in `try/except` that continues, or a second load path skips it. If only hosted models are used, answer yes citing the config that shows that.","met":"yes","evidence":"release/manifest.yaml:41","quote":"provider: anthropic","counter_search":"Searched all model load sites and dependency list; no self-hosted weights loader.","note":"Both models hosted through provider SDK; no local weights or adapters."},{"id":"C03.5","check":"A mismatch blocks or quarantines the deployment, not only logs it.","verify":"1) Find the code that handles a manifest or digest mismatch. 2) Check it blocks or quarantines: non-zero exit, admission deny, refusal to start, scale to zero. 3) Answer no if the mismatch branch only logs, warns, or emits a metric and continues, or an error in the check lets deployment proceed.","met":"no","evidence":"app/startup.py:43","quote":"log.error(\"running state differs from release manifest: %s\", \", \".join(mismatches))","counter_search":"","note":"Mismatch logs then continues with old manifest type ID, no block or quarantine."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Check the running setup against the approved manifest, and emit the matching agent-type-id"],"also_affects":["C04"],"summary":"Startup detects mismatches but continues under the approved type identity.","next_step":"Block mismatches and compute identity from independently observed running artifacts.","lead_role":"infrastructure"},{"item":"C04","gate":"G2","title":"Detect drift per agent","requirement":"Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline. Simulate a prompt edit, an added tool, and a looser egress rule. Check that each one raises an alert and gets the documented response — block, quarantine, or rollback — within a set time.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Hosted model changing behind a fixed name","owner":"C05"},{"problem":"A tool server changing its description or schema after approval","owner":"E03"},{"problem":"Who may change production config, and emergency change records","owner":"C02"},{"problem":"Manifest missing components that define the release","owner":"C01"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/startup.py","line":43,"note":"Known local drift only logged; no operator alert response or response time bound."}],"checks":[{"id":"C04.1","check":"A drift check compares running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against the approved baseline, with each of these covered.","verify":"1) Find the drift check job or tool. 2) List what it compares: images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, self-hosted weights. 3) Check each is compared with the approved baseline, not with the live state itself. 4) Answer no if any category is missing or excluded. Answer unknown if drift detection runs in an outside platform.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Read running_state_mismatches and MCP pin checks; startup covers subset but platform scheduled drift comparison of network/IAM/harness not supplied."},{"id":"C04.2","check":"The drift check runs per agent deployment, on a schedule or on change events.","verify":"1) Find what triggers the drift check: cron or CI schedule, admission webhook, or change events. 2) Check it runs for each agent deployment, not once for the fleet or only by hand. 3) Answer no if it is manual-only or covers only some deployments. Answer unknown if scheduling is set outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Searched CI schedules, deployment and startup; no runtime drift schedule supplied, external platform scheduling unknown."},{"id":"C04.3","check":"Detected drift triggers an alert and a set response (block, quarantine, or rollback) defined in config, with a time limit.","verify":"1) Open the drift check's result handling. 2) Check drift raises an alert and triggers a response set in config: block, quarantine, or rollback. 3) Check a time limit is set. 4) Answer no if drift only logs, the response or time limit is missing, or a check error is treated as no drift.","met":"no","evidence":"app/startup.py:43","quote":"log.error(\"running state differs from release manifest: %s\", \", \".join(mismatches))","counter_search":"","note":"Known local drift only logged; no operator alert response or response time bound."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Check that each one raises an alert and gets the documented response — block, quarantine, or rollback — within a set time"],"also_affects":["C03"],"summary":"Detected local drift only logs without a bounded response.","next_step":"Add scheduled comparison and named alert with block quarantine or rollback deadline.","lead_role":"operations"},{"item":"C05","gate":"G2","title":"Control dependency, model, and training changes","requirement":"Pin dependency versions. Where supported, also pin each model's base version, checkpoint or weights, and fine-tune or adapter version. Before promotion, link any changed training run, dataset, or training code or config to the model it produced and to its test results. Record the model version actually served, when the runtime or provider shares it, separately from the name you requested. Before loading weights, adapters, or datasets you host, check their signature against an approved signer (for example, with OpenSSF Model Signing). Also check their file format. Pickle-based formats can run code when loaded, so they need an approved exception and a scan. Test swapping a model, checkpoint, or adapter, and check that it triggers review and re-testing. Some remote services or names can change behind a fixed name. For those, record missing training and version details clearly. Watch available version metadata and provider notices, and decide when to re-test or stop using the model. A local config hash alone can't prove remote behavior is unchanged. A pinned snapshot fixes the weights, not the provider's serving systems, which can change under the same ID. Keep scheduled re-testing.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Tool or MCP server approved without reviewing publisher, permissions, or vulnerabilities","owner":"E02"},{"problem":"Container image not pinned by digest or signature-checked","owner":"B10"},{"problem":"Rollback setup naming a hosted model that is retired","owner":"C07"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"Dockerfile","line":7,"note":"Direct dependencies pinned but no lockfile for transitive dependencies or build backend; Dockerfile/CI resolve dependencies afresh."}],"checks":[{"id":"C05.1","check":"Dependency versions are pinned with exact versions or hashes in lockfiles, with no ranges or floating tags.","verify":"1) Open every dependency file and lockfile (`requirements*.txt`, `poetry.lock`, `package-lock.json`, `go.sum`) plus Dockerfile `FROM` and install lines. 2) Look for ranges (`^`, `~`, `>=`, `*`), missing lockfiles, and floating tags. 3) Answer no if any dependency is unpinned, including install commands in Dockerfiles or CI scripts that bypass the lockfile.","met":"no","evidence":"Dockerfile:7","quote":"RUN pip install --target /opt/site .","counter_search":"","note":"Direct dependencies pinned but no lockfile for transitive dependencies or build backend; Dockerfile/CI resolve dependencies afresh."},{"id":"C05.2","check":"Model IDs in config are pinned snapshots (plus checkpoint, weights, and adapter versions where supported), not aliases such as 'latest'.","verify":"1) Find every model ID in config, env files, and code defaults. 2) Follow env vars to their fallback value. 3) Answer no if any is an alias (`-latest`, undated name), falls back to one when unset, or leaves out the checkpoint, weights, or adapter version where one is used and the provider supports pinning it.","met":"yes","evidence":"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:43","quote":"value: \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"","counter_search":"Checked settings _env requires model and deployment supplies snapshots; no adapters or alternate model routes.","note":"Both model IDs pinned dated snapshots without alias fallback."},{"id":"C05.3","check":"Self-hosted weights, adapters, and datasets have their signatures checked against an approved signer before loading, and loading stops if the check fails.","verify":"1) Find load paths for self-hosted weights, adapters, and datasets. 2) Check a signature check against an approved signer (for example OpenSSF Model Signing, `cosign verify` with a pinned identity) runs before loading. 3) Answer no if any path skips it, any signer is accepted, or a failure is caught and loading continues. If nothing is self-hosted, answer yes citing the config that shows that.","met":"yes","evidence":"release/manifest.yaml:41","quote":"provider: anthropic","counter_search":"Searched loaders and fine-tune paths; only hosted provider calls.","note":"No self-hosted weights adapters or datasets to load."},{"id":"C05.4","check":"Pickle-based model formats are refused at load unless an approved exception and scan are recorded.","verify":"1) Search for pickle-capable loads: `pickle.load`, `torch.load`, `joblib.load`, `.pkl`, `.pt`, `.bin` files. 2) Check the loader refuses these formats unless an approved exception and scan are recorded. 3) Answer no if any pickle-based load runs without that check.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/main.py:96","quote":"client = AsyncAnthropic()","counter_search":"Searched pickle torch joblib pkl pt bin and trust_remote_code; no unsafe model loader found.","note":"Model access uses hosted client; no pickle model load path."},{"id":"C05.5","check":"The model version the provider or runtime reports serving is recorded separately from the requested model name.","verify":"1) Find model call sites