recovery handling, not an observed unsafe replay."],"violates":["Keep an approved recovery setup and show that rollback works.","Account for changed credentials, memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work."],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Recovery setup and hosted model retirement evidence are not supplied.","next_step":"Provide approved rollback procedure covering identity, memory, pending work and model availability.","lead_role":"operations","challenge":{"verdict":"failed","note":"C07 fails because the repository supplies neither an approved recovery setup and rollback procedure nor explicit recovery handling for persisted state."}},{"item":"C08","gate":"G2","title":"Connect configuration to execution","requirement":"From a trace, look up the release manifest, the context sizes at each decision, and any prompts a parent passed to a sub-agent. Keep these links for the full audit retention period. Control access to sensitive artifacts.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Context size not measured or logged for each action decision","owner":"R07"},{"problem":"Action records missing any of the six identity fields","owner":"A02"},{"problem":"Manifest missing components that define the release","owner":"C01"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/extractor.py","line":79,"note":"Both model paths record decision context measure with trace and identity."}],"checks":[{"id":"C08.1","check":"Each trace or audit record carries the agent-type-id or manifest reference that resolves to the stored release manifest.","verify":"1) Open the trace or audit record writer. 2) Check every record carries `agent.type.id` or a manifest reference. 3) Check that value is the key of a stored manifest. 4) Answer no if the field is missing on some paths (errors, background jobs) or holds a value that resolves to no stored manifest.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Read audit type IDs and manifest file; external stored manifest-by-type archive not supplied, resolver cannot be established."},{"id":"C08.2","check":"The context size at each model decision is recorded in the trace.","verify":"1) Find model call sites and their spans. 2) Look for the context size recorded per call (for example `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens` or a context-length attribute). 3) Answer no if it is missing on any model call path, including retries and sub-agents.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/extractor.py:79","quote":"self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,","counter_search":"Inspected main and helper calls and audit persistence; measures recorded for each successful decision, missing counts explicitly unavailable.","note":"Both model paths record decision context measure with trace and identity."},{"id":"C08.3","check":"Prompts passed from a parent to a sub-agent are stored and linked from the trace.","verify":"1) Find sub-agent spawn code. 2) Check the parent's prompt is stored and the trace holds a link to it (ID, hash, or URI). 3) Answer no if the prompt is not stored, prompt capture is off, or the trace has no link.","met":"no","evidence":"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:66","quote":"- name: OTEL_INSTRUMENTATION_GENAI_CAPTURE_MESSAGE_CONTENT","counter_search":"","note":"Capture set false and extractor prompt ref is span ID with no stored text."},{"id":"C08.4","check":"Storage config keeps manifests, traces, and these links for at least the audit retention period, and limits access to sensitive artifacts by role.","verify":"1) Find storage config for manifests, traces, and prompt links: bucket lifecycle rules, log retention, TTLs. 2) Check retention covers the audit period for all of them. 3) Check IAM limits sensitive artifacts by role. 4) Answer no if any has a shorter TTL, no retention, or broad read access. Answer unknown if storage is configured outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Inspected audit table grants and release artifact references; backend manifest/trace/prompt retention and restricted artifact archive policy outside repository."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["any prompts a parent passed to a sub-agent"],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Trace links cannot recover the uncaptured parent prompts.","next_step":"Persist protected parent prompt artifacts and retain trace and manifest links together.","lead_role":"operations"},{"item":"E01","gate":"G2","title":"Map shared responsibilities","requirement":"List the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, and audit services. For each control that applies, name the owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side. Keep evidence for both halves. Using an upstream service doesn't make its controls N/A.","not_covered":[{"problem":"A tool call that skips the MCP gateway or reaches a tool server directly","owner":"E06"},{"problem":"A vendor service dropping agent or tenant identity from its records","owner":"E10"},{"problem":"Tool or MCP server approved without vetting or pinning","owner":"E02"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"release/manifest.yaml","line":63,"note":"Manifest covers ERP and models but omits complete STS, OIDC, payment, Slack proxy and audit-service boundary inventory."}],"checks":[{"id":"E01.1","check":"An inventory file lists the outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, and audit services.","verify":"1) Find the inventory file. 2) Check each category the agent uses is listed: outside tools, MCP servers, peer agents, sub-agents, registries, identity services, gateways, stop channels, audit services. 3) Answer no if no inventory exists or a category the agent uses is missing.","met":"no","evidence":"release/manifest.yaml:63","quote":"mcp_servers:","counter_search":"","note":"Manifest covers ERP and models but omits complete STS, OIDC, payment,