handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/extractor.py:43","quote":"budget.check_subagent()","counter_search":"Checked extraction request and main endpoints; no serialized peer-action queue or callback nonce protocol, side effects from widened role owned by E08.","note":"Local read-extraction request is a direct fresh call with shared invocation cap; no external replayable action request endpoint exists."},{"id":"E07.4","check":"Peer message content is handled as untrusted data and is not placed into system or instruction prompts.","verify":"1) Trace peer message content to the prompt builder. 2) Check it goes into user or tool-result content as untrusted data. 3) Answer no if any path places it into the system prompt or an instruction template.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/loop.py:101","quote":"return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"content\": redact_for_model(output)}","counter_search":"Traced extraction tool wrapper through execute_tool and parent messages; no parent prompt interpolation.","note":"Child response returns as tool-result data, never trusted system instructions."},{"id":"E07.5","check":"Callback and webhook URLs are checked against SSRF, with private and metadata addresses blocked.","verify":"1) Find code that calls callback or webhook URLs from peers. 2) Check URL validation blocks private, loopback, link-local, and metadata addresses (169.254.169.254). 3) Answer no if any callback is fetched without the check, or only the hostname text is checked and not the resolved address.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/main.py:119","quote":"app.include_router(ingest.router)","counter_search":"Inspected all endpoints and clients; fixed ERP/payment/Slack/STS URLs, no agent-to-agent callback target.","note":"Only local peer calls; no peer-supplied callback or webhook URL is fetched."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Validate message types and schemas"],"also_affects":["R01"],"summary":"Local child messages accept incomplete and incorrectly typed line items.","next_step":"Enforce strict message schemas and reject invalid values before parent use.","lead_role":"agent_team"},{"item":"E08","gate":"G1","title":"Bounded delegated authority","requirement":"Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task. Enforce each child's role and any explicit approval from a higher authority. A parent must not gain a power it was denied just by asking a more powerful peer to act. Narrow credentials at each hop, for example with token exchange or transaction tokens. Authorize based on the original subject (the user or system whose authority is used) and the current actor. Earlier actors in a delegation chain are for the record only, not a reason to grant access. Test that escalation attempt.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Approvals that can be replayed or aren't tied to exact arguments","owner":"B06"},{"problem":"Prompt a parent gave a sub-agent not recorded","owner":"A06"},{"problem":"Children still running after the parent is stopped","owner":"E09"},{"problem":"Replayed or faked peer-agent messages","owner":"E07"},{"problem":"No limit on how many sub-agents a run can start","owner":"B07"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/extractor.py","line":45,"note":"EXTRACTOR_ROLE line_item_extractor does not match configured extractor; registry fallback grants full procurement tools and shared broker authority."}],"checks":[{"id":"E08.1","check":"Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.","verify":"1) Find where a child agent gets its credential. 2) Check it is a narrowed token for the task (token exchange, transaction token, scoped-down role). 3) Answer no if any spawn path passes the parent's token, API key, or full role, or the child inherits the parent's environment credentials.","met":"no","evidence":"app/extractor.py:45","quote":"registry = build_registry(EXTRACTOR_ROLE, ident, self.deps)","counter_search":"","note":"EXTRACTOR_ROLE line_item_extractor does not match configured extractor; registry fallback grants full procurement tools and shared broker authority."},{"id":"E08.2","check":"Authorization at the action uses the original subject and the current actor, and earlier actors in the delegation chain never add access.","verify":"1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.","met":"no","evidence":"app/identity.py:95","quote":"key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)","counter_search":"","note":"Token cache omits original subject/current actor and child role; delegated actions can reuse another actor token within tenant."},{"id":"E08.3","check":"An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.","verify":"1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.","met":"no","evidence":"app/tools/__init__.py:69","quote":"allowed = roles.get(role, roles[DEFAULT_ROLE])","counter_search":"","note":"Unknown child role defaults to parent full privileges instead of fail-closed task role; child can perform ERP writes unrelated to extraction."},{"id":"E08.4","check":"Downstream services reject the parent's token when the child presents it (audience-bound tokens).","verify":"1) Find how child tokens are issued and how downstream services validate tokens. 2) Check tokens are audience-bound and services verify `aud`. 3) Answer no if audience is unset, a wildcard, or not checked. Answer unknown if downstream services are outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Read broker audience exchange and child shared principal; external receiving-service audience and child-versus-parent authorization validation not supplied."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task"],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Extractor role mismatch grants child the full procurement authority.","next_step":"Reject unknown roles, align extractor role names and scope child credentials to original subject/current actor.","lead_role":"agent_team"},{"item":"E09","gate":"G1","title":"Recursive shutdown","requirement":"Run a drill across a parent, nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks, where they exist. Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time. It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts. Record how outside effects that already happened are reconciled.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Agent able to disable or delay its own stop","owner":"R11"},{"problem":"No way to cut off the agent's access without cutting off the user","owner":"B04"},{"problem":"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type","owner":"E12"},{"problem":"Sub-agent given powers beyond its task","owner":"E08"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/extractor.py","line":64,"note":"Extractor loop never checks root stop flag and no root cancellation propagates into child."}],"checks":[{"id":"E09.1","check":"A stop signal from the root reaches every descendant: nested children, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks.","verify":"1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check it reaches nested children, remote workers, queued jobs, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks (cancel calls, MCP `notifications/cancelled`). 3) Answer no if any of these that exists in the code is not reached, or stop only sets an in-process flag that remote workers never read.","met":"no","evidence":"app/extractor.py:64","quote":"for _turn in range(MAX_TURNS):","counter_search":"","note":"Extractor loop never checks root stop flag and no root cancellation propagates into child."},{"id":"E09.2","check":"Stopping revokes descendants' credentials or leases, and leases or tokens are short-lived, so a disconnected worker loses authority within the stop time limit.","verify":"1) Open the stop path and credential issuing code. 2) Check stopping revokes descendants' tokens or leases. 3) Check token or lease lifetime fits within the stop time limit. 4) Answer no if no revocation exists, or tokens are long-lived so a disconnected worker keeps authority.","met":"no","evidence":"app/identity.py:98","quote":"return cached.value","counter_search":"","note":"Child shares broker credentials; stop path has no descendant credential revocation or bounded leases."},{"id":"E09.3","check":"Queues and schedulers refuse new work, retries, and restarts for a stopped tree.","verify":"1) Find queue consumers, schedulers, and retry logic. 2) Check each looks up the stopped state before running new work, retries, or restarts. 3) Answer no if any consumer, retry decorator, or restart policy runs without that check.","met":"no","evidence":"app/extractor.py:74","quote":"response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)","counter_search":"","note":"Child starts additional calls and SDK retries without stopped-tree lookup."},{"id":"E09.4","check":"Outside effects already completed are recorded for reconciliation.","verify":"1) Open the stop path. 2) Check it records outside effects already completed (tool calls, writes, sent messages) for reconciliation. 3) Answer no if nothing is recorded, or only in-flight work is listed.","met":"no","evidence":"app/extractor.py:96","quote":"results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))","counter_search":"","note":"Child may have outside effects through expanded role; no completed-effect reconciliation ledger on stop."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time"],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Root stop never reaches child calls or revokes child authority.","next_step":"Propagate cancellation, block new child work, revoke leases and reconcile completed effects.","lead_role":"operations"},{"item":"E10","gate":"G1","title":"Audit across service boundaries","requirement":"Rebuild a run across the gateway, tool services, and delegated workers, with all six identity fields kept. Check that the agent can't erase or rewrite its audit history, either directly or by asking a more powerful tool or peer. Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Audit retention, access, redaction, or export rules missing","owner":"E11"},{"problem":"Authorization decisions missing the policy version in the run record","owner":"R13"},{"problem":"Instance or tenant labels taken from what the model supplies","owner":"A04"},{"problem":"Recovery checkpoints not tamper-evident","owner":"R14"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"migrations/001_init.sql","line":121,"note":"Audit grants append only to runtime role after REVOKE ALL."}],"checks":[{"id":"E10.1","check":"The gateway, tool services, and delegated workers each write audit records with all six identity fields and the shared trace context.","verify":"1) Find audit writers in the gateway, tool services, and delegated workers. 2) Check each writes all six identity fields and the shared trace context. 3) Answer no if any component writes records without them or starts a new trace. Answer unknown if a component's code is outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"[challenge: unclear] The local audit writer inserts and validates all six identity fields; delegated children retain the parent's trace_id. The ERP call explicitly carries only tenant and run_id in metadata. External gateway and tool-service audit writers and token claims are absent, so their six-field records and shared trace cannot be verified."},{"id":"E10.2","check":"The agent's credentials have no permission to delete, update, or overwrite audit records (for example an append-only or WORM store with IAM denies).","verify":"1) Find the agent's IAM role or database grants and the audit store config. 2) Check the agent has no delete, update, or overwrite rights (`DeleteObject`, overwriting `PutObject`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`) and the store is append-only or WORM (Object Lock). 3) Answer no if the agent's credentials can delete or rewrite records, or grant `*`. Answer unknown if these are set outside this repo.","met":"yes","evidence":"migrations/001_init.sql:121","quote":"GRANT SELECT, INSERT ON audit_events TO procurement_agent;","counter_search":"Checked all grants; runtime gets no UPDATE DELETE TRUNCATE or schema owner role in repository.","note":"Audit grants append only to runtime role after REVOKE ALL."},{"id":"E10.3","check":"No tool or peer the agent can call is able to delete or rewrite audit records on its behalf, or such requests are held for approval under B05.","verify":"1) List the tools and peers the agent can call. 2) For each, check whether it can delete or rewrite audit records (database admin, log management, storage tools). 3) Answer no if any can and such requests are not held for approval under B05.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"[challenge: unclear] The local registry offers document, extraction, ERP, payment, Slack and memory tools, with no local audit-management operation. Refreshed ERP operations are accepted without pin verification and pre