essage and database is not a stored mapping to Slack's receipt and the verified run identity/correlation ID. Budget-stop notifications also discard Slack receipts at agent/app/loop.py:180."],"violates":["Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it."],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Append-only local receipts exist but cross-service audit coverage is external.","next_step":"Supply gateway and vendor identity-linked records and audit-management permission evidence.","lead_role":"infrastructure","challenge":{"verdict":"failed","note":"E10 fails because approval notifications cross the Slack boundary without storing the returned vendor receipt linked to the initiating run identity and correlation ID."}},{"item":"E11","gate":"G2","title":"Protect shared evidence","requirement":"Set rules for how long audit records are kept, who can see them, what is redacted, how their integrity is checked, and how they are exported and restored. Test pulling up a past run, and test that missing records or a broken pipeline get noticed. Keep records long enough for investigations and for the law. For example, the EU AI Act requires providers and deployers of high-risk systems to keep automatically generated logs for at least six months (Articles 19 and 26). High-impact actions must fail closed when required audit capture isn't working.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Agent able to erase or rewrite its own audit history","owner":"E10"},{"problem":"Run record missing denials, approvals, or results","owner":"R13"},{"problem":"Secrets left in tool output, responses, or normal logs","owner":"R03"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/audit.py","line":116,"note":"Sensitive payload values redacted and table read access granted to named agent/ops roles."}],"checks":[{"id":"E11.1","check":"Audit retention is set in config to cover the investigation window and the legal minimum (for example at least six months for EU AI Act high-risk systems).","verify":"1) Find retention settings for audit storage: bucket lifecycle rules, log retention days, TTLs. 2) Check the value covers the investigation window and the legal minimum (for example six months for EU AI Act high-risk systems). 3) Answer no if retention is shorter or unset. Answer unknown if audit storage is configured outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"[challenge: unclear] Audit records use an external Postgres service. Searches of agent/ for retention, lifecycle, TTL, and audit storage configuration found no audit retention period or investigation window. The database lifecycle configuration is not supplied, so its retention cannot be established."},{"id":"E11.2","check":"Access to audit records is limited by role, and redaction rules apply to sensitive fields.","verify":"1) Find IAM policies or ACLs on audit storage. 2) Check reads are limited by role. 3) Check redaction rules apply to sensitive fields. 4) Answer no if read access is broad (`*`, all engineers) or no redaction exists.","met":"no","evidence":"app/redact.py:56, app/audit.py:116","quote":"        return {k: redact_value(v) for k, v in value.items()}\n        json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),","counter_search":"Checked REVOKE/GRANT and redactor; no broad public/all-engineer audit read grant supplied.","note":"[challenge] SQL grants audit reads to named agent and ops roles, but sensitive-field redaction is bypassable. Dictionary keys are preserved and values are redacted without their field names. A payload containing {\"password\": \"plain-secret\"} is stored unchanged: the bare value matches none of the configured secret or account patterns. Nested tool arguments and results pass through this same function."},{"id":"E11.3","check":"Integrity protection (hash chain, signatures, or WORM) plus sequence numbers or delivery receipts let missing records be detected, with an alert on gaps or pipeline