 preserved and values are redacted without their field names. A payload containing {\"password\": \"plain-secret\"} is stored unchanged: the bare value matches none of the configured secret or account patterns. Nested tool arguments and results pass through this same function.","app/audit.py:91, app/loop.py:99, app/main.py:196 The complete writer and schema use random IDs and parent links without sequence numbers or persisted delivery receipts. Runtime append-only grants do not implement hash-chain verification or missing-event detection. Result hashes are computed but no audit integrity verifier consumes them. Searches across agent/ for integrity, sequence, receipt, alert, and audit consumers found no gap or pipeline-failure alert; the health endpoint returns success without checking audit capture. External infrastructure is unspecified, but the required local detection and verification pieces are absent."],"violates":["what is redacted","how their integrity is checked","test that missing records or a broken pipeline get noticed"],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Local audit capture fails closed but shared retention integrity is external.","next_step":"Provide retention integrity gap-alert export and restore controls from audit platform.","lead_role":"infrastructure","challenge":{"verdict":"failed","note":"E11 fails because sensitive-field redaction is bypassable and audit integrity verification and missing-record or pipeline-failure alerts are absent."}},{"item":"E12","gate":"G3","title":"Fleet incident response","requirement":"Run a drill where a shared tool or agent type is compromised. Find the affected instances and tenants. Quarantine the dependency, revoke the access involved, stop affected work, and alert the named responders. Check that alerts about abuse across agents, and about budgets, reach the team that can act. Name who decides whether to report outside the organization and share information.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Kill switch for a single agent not drilled","owner":"R11"},{"problem":"No owner named on each side of a shared control","owner":"E01"},{"problem":"Tool or MCP server approved without vetting or pinning","owner":"E02"},{"problem":"Budget and rate limits not enforced outside the model","owner":"B07"}],"rating":"needs_evidence","confidence":"medium","evidence":[],"checks":[],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":[],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Fleet compromise response drill and reporting decision owners are not supplied.","next_step":"Run shared-dependency incident drill with impact lookup revocation containment and named responders.","lead_role":"security"},{"item":"R01","gate":"G2","title":"Validate every input boundary, including API responses","requirement":"List every input the agent receives. That includes API responses (errors and streamed content too), tool and connector output, incoming webhooks and callbacks, messages from other agents, user input, fetched pages, files, and retrieved chunks. Authenticate each sender (prove who sent it), and verify signatures where they exist. Treat content as untrusted even when it comes from an authenticated service or an internal one. Before content reaches the model or runs anywhere, check its type, schema, and size. Also check its content for attack payloads and hidden prompt-injection instructions. Reject or hold aside bad payloads. If a required check fails to run, don't let unchecked content through. Test broken, oversized, faked, and hostile responses from each integration.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Injected instructions in valid content reaching forbidden tools unblocked","owner":"R02"},{"problem":"Hidden instructions in tool names, descriptions, or schemas","owner":"E04"},{"problem":"Replayed peer-agent requests with no freshness or nonce check","owner":"E07"},{"problem":"Secrets leaking into outputs or normal logs","owner":"R03"},{"problem":"Unapproved sources able to add documents to the retrieval corpus","owner":"R04"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/loop.py","line":101,"note":"Inputs: user tasks, mail, Slack callbacks, ERP success/error, payment and Slack responses, memory and extractor output. ERP and memory reach model after redaction without complete schema/content validation."}],"checks":[{"id":"R01.1","check":"Every input path passes through validation code: API and tool responses (including errors and streams), webhooks and callbacks, agent messages, user input, fetched pages, files, and retrieved chunks.","verify":"1) List every input: tool and API responses (errors, streams), webhooks, agent messages, user input, fetched pages, files, retrieved chunks. 2) Trace each to where it enters the model context. 3) Answer no if any path, including error bodies, stream chunks, or a second handler, reaches the model without passing validation code.","met":"no","evidence":"app/loop.py:101","quote":"return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"content\": redact_for_model(output)}","counter_search":"","note":"Inputs: user tasks, mail, Slack callbacks, ERP success/error, payment and Slack responses, memory and extractor output. ERP and memory reach model after redaction without complete schema/content validation."},{"id":"R01.2","check":"Type, schema, and size checks run before content, including streamed chunks, is added to the model context or executed.","verify":"1) Find validation code (`pydantic`, `zod`, `jsonschema`, size limits, `max_bytes`, content-type checks). 2) Check it runs before content is added to the context or executed, including per stream chunk. 3) Answer no if validation runs after use, only on success responses, streams skip it, or there is no size limit.","met":"no","evidence":"app/loop.py:83","quote":"output = await tool.invoke(use.input, ident)","counter_search":"","note":"Model arguments passed to integrations without enforcing declared JSON schemas; ERP response structuredContent has no schema check."},{"id":"R01.3","check":"Senders are authenticated, and signatures are verified where the integration provides them, including for internal and authenticated services.","verify":"1) Find webhook, callback, and inbound handlers. 2) Check sender authentication and signature verification (`hmac.compare_digest`, `verify_signature`, mTLS). 3) Answer no if any handler skips it, internal services are trusted without auth, the signature is compared with `==`, or a verify failure is caught and processing continues.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/main.py:171","quote":"if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Signature\", \"\")):","counter_search":"Traced main and ingest handlers; verification failures reject before processing, HTTP clients verify TLS by default.","note":"Slack/mail signatures and caller JWT verification authenticate inbound paths."},{"id":"R01.4","check":"Content is also screened for attack payloads or injection instructions, not only for structure.","verify":"1) Find content screening (injection detector, pattern rules, classifier, encoded-payload checks). 2) Check it runs on content, not just schema. 3) Answer no if only type or schema checks exist, or screening covers some inputs (for example user input) but not tool output, fetched pages, or retrieved chunks.","met":"no","evidence":"app/ingest.py:97","quote":"if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:","counter_search":"","note":"Accepted message/rfc822 mail extracted then excluded from content scanner; ERP responses and model task text also lack screening."},{"id":"R01.5","check":"Bad payloads are rejected or held aside, and if a check errors, times out, or is skipped, the content is blocked.","verify":"1) Find what happens when validation fails or errors. 2) Read `try`/`except`, `catch`, timeout, and default branches. 3) Answer no if failures log and continue, an error or timeout passes content through, a feature flag can skip checks, or bad content is truncated and still used.","met":"no","evidence":"app/ingest.py:101","quote":"return text","counter_search":"","note":"message/rfc822 reaches accepted storage with content screening skipped; required boundary screening not fail-closed."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Before content reaches the model or runs anywhere, check its type, schema, and size"],"also_affects":["E07","R11"],"summary":"Email and ERP inputs bypass complete boundary validation.","next_step":"Validate all schemas, sizes and content before model or integration use.","lead_role":"agent_team"},{"item":"R02","gate":"G2","title":"Separate data from instructions and test injection containment","requirement":"Keep API responses, connector messages, and other outside content out of trusted system and policy channels. Label where each piece came from and how much it is trusted. Test prompt injection in responses that pass schema checks. Include free-text fields, error messages, documents, and tool output. Checks and channel separation can't guarantee that prompt injection is prevented. So show that credential limits, tool permissions, and destructive-action gates still block harm if the model follows an injected instruction. Repeat each attack and include adaptive versions. One failed attempt makes a defense look stronger than it is. B05 covers agents that combine untrusted input, sensitive access, and outside actions.","not_covered":[{"problem":"Missing type, schema, or size checks on API responses","owner":"R01"},{"problem":"Hidden instructions in tool names, descriptions, or schemas","owner":"E04"},{"problem":"One run planting instructions in another run's memory","owner":"R05"},{"problem":"Generated output run as SQL or shell without parameterizing","owner":"R03"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/loop.py","line":174,"note":"Tool results enter user tool-result channel; fixed system prompt separate."}],"checks":[{"id":"R02.1","check":"Outside content (API responses, tool output, documents, connector messages) goes into user or tool message roles, never into the system or policy prompt.","verify":"1) Find where model requests are built (`system=`, `messages`, `role: system`, prompt templates). 2) Trace outside content (tool output, documents, API responses) into the request. 3) Answer no if any outside content is concatenated into the system or policy prompt, including retrieved context or tool descriptions from servers.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/loop.py:174","quote":"messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})","counter_search":"Checked parent and extractor request construction and local tool descriptions; no external text interpolated into system prompt.","note":"Tool results enter user tool-result channel; fixed system prompt separate."},{"id":"R02.2","check":"Each piece of outside content carries a source and trust label in the model request.","verify":"1) Find where outside content is wrapped before the model request. 2) Check each piece carries a source and trust label. 3) Answer no if some sources (for example tool output or retrieved chunks) have no label, or labels are set by the content itself.","met":"no","evidence":"app/mcp_client.py:131","quote":"return result.get(\"structuredContent\") or result.get(\"content\")","counter_search":"","note":"Raw ERP payload lacks source and trust envelope; generic tool-result ID does not label trust."},{"id":"R02.3","check":"Credential limits, tool permissions, and B05 action gates block the actions an injected instruction could cause, enforced in code the model cannot change.","verify":"1) List actions an injected instruction could cause: sends, writes, deletes, fetches. 2) Check each is blocked by credential scope, tool allowlist, or B05 gate in harness code. 3) Answer no if any harmful action is stopped only by the model declining, or the limit can be changed by tool arguments or model output.","met":"no","evidence":"app/gate.py:35","quote":"if not operation.startswith(self.erp_read_prefixes):","counter_search":"","note":"Injected instruction can select permitted vendor/invoice write operation; narrow gate does not contain harm."},{"id":"R02.4","check":"Containment does not rely on prompt wording, delimiters, or an injection detector.","verify":"1) Find the defenses relied on for injection. 2) Check whether removing prompt wording, delimiters, or the detector would leave harmful actions blocked. 3) Answer no if containment depends on system-prompt rules, delimiter tags, or a detector, with no code-level block behind it.","met":"no","evidence":"app/gate.py:37","quote":"return Decision(True, \"erp read operation\", self.version)","counter_search":"","note":"Prompt forbids bank changes while gate admits vendor.update_remit_to without code-level block."},{"id":"R02.5","check":"Injection tests repeat each fixture a set number of times, include adaptive variants and schema-valid payloads, and report success rates.","verify":"1) Find injection tests (`tests/`, eval suites, red-team fixtures). 2) Check fixtures repeat a set number of times, include adaptive variants and schema-valid payloads, and report a success rate. 3) Answer no if each test runs once, uses only malformed inputs, or reports pass/fail. Answer unknown if tests live outside this repo.","met":"no","evidence":"tests/test_gate.py:81","quote":"def test_injection_in_plain_text_is_rejected():","counter_search":"","note":"Only a single detector test; no repeated adaptive schema-valid end-to-end containment attempts or success-rate reporting."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["So show that credential limits, tool permissions, and destructive-action gates still block harm if the model follows an injected instruction"],"also_affects":["B05"],"summary":"Separated message roles do not contain destructive injected calls.","next_step":"Label all outputs and block forbidden actions independently; repeat adaptive injection tests.","lead_role":"security"},{"item":"R03","gate":"G2","title":"Prevent output and log leakage","requirement":"Remove secrets and limit sensitive data before tool output, debug output, or responses reach the model, outside recipients, or normal logs. Some clients fetch URLs on their own when they display output, such as Markdown images and link previews. These can leak data without any tool call, so block them or allow only approved URLs. Check generated output before it goes into SQL, a shell, an HTML page, or anything else that runs it. Use parameterized queries and commands (for example, argument lists for shell calls), and the right escaping for each context. Test with fake secrets and injection payloads. Confirm that leaks and unintended execution are blocked, and that redacted audit evidence is kept.","not_covered":[{"problem":"A tool call sending data to an unapproved destination","owner":"B09"},{"problem":"Long-lived secrets checked into config or baked into images","owner":"B03"},{"problem":"Incoming hostile payloads not validated","owner":"R01"},{"problem":"Retrieval returning another tenant's documents","owner":"R04"}],"rating":"gap","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/redact.py","line":100,"note":"Logging filter returns after sanitizing msg/args, leaving formatted exception traceback text unredacted; provider counting errors log with exc_info=True at app/context_size.py:73."}],"checks":[{"id":"R03.1","check":"Secrets and sensitive fields are redacted from tool output, debug output, and error text before they reach the model, outside recipients, or normal logs.","verify":"1) Find redaction code (`redact`, `mask`, secret patterns) and where tool output, errors, and debug text go. 2) Check redaction runs before the model, outside recipients, and logs. 3) Answer no if any path skips it, such as error messages, exception traces, debug logging, or `logger.info(response)` before redaction.","met":"no","evidence":"app/redact.py:100","quote":"return True","counter_search":"","note":"Logging filter redacts only record.msg and record.args; exception traceback is formatted afterward and remains unredacted. context_size logs provider count errors with exc_info=True, which may include response secrets."},{"id":"R03.2","check":"The display client blocks auto-fetched URLs (Markdown images, link previews) or allows only approved hosts.","verify":"1) Find the display client or renderer (Markdown render, link unfurl, image tags). 2) Check auto-fetched URLs are blocked or limited to approved hosts (CSP `img-src`, URL allowlist). 3) Answer no if Markdown images or previews load any URL. Answer unknown if the display client is outside this repo.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Read Slack post disables unfurls and strips links, but general final-response display renderer is outside repository; cannot verify auto-fetch restrictions for every client."},{"id":"R03.3","check":"Generated SQL uses parameterized queries, shell calls use argument lists with no string-built commands, and HTML output is escaped for its context.","verify":"1) Search for SQL, shell, and HTML built from generated output (`execute(f`, `+ query`, `shell=True`, `exec(`, `innerHTML`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `|safe`). 2) Check for parameters, argument lists, and context escaping. 3) Answer no if any query or command is string-built, uses `shell=True` or `sh -c` with model input, or HTML is unescaped.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/tools/memory.py:76","quote":"await pool.execute(","counter_search":"Searched execute fstrings, shell=True, subprocess and HTML renders; queries use positional parameters throughout.","note":"All model-derived SQL values parameterized; no shell or HTML execution sink."},{"id":"R03.4","check":"Redacted audit evidence is kept rather than discarded.","verify":"1) Find redaction code and audit logging. 2) Check redacted records are written to an audit store. 3) Answer no if redaction drops the whole record, or the evidence is discarded instead of kept.","met":"yes","evidence":"app/audit.py:116","quote":"json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),","counter_search":"Read audit insert and callers; redaction retains record instead of dropping evidence.","note":"Audit stores redacted payload while retaining event structure and identity."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":["Remove secrets and limit sensitive data before tool output, debug output, or responses reach the model, outside recipients, or normal logs"],"also_affects":[],"summary":"Formatted exception tracebacks bypass the normal logging redaction filter.","next_step":"Redact formatted exception text and verify all output sinks with fake-secret markers.","lead_role":"agent_team"},{"item":"R04","gate":"G2","title":"Retrieval-corpus integrity","requirement":"The retrieval corpus is the set of documents the agent searches for context. Its index stores those documents, or smaller passages called chunks, in a search engine or vector database. Limit which identities and sources can add or change content there. For each chunk, keep its source, when it was added, its trust level, and its access permissions. Enforce the requesting tenant's access when searching. Test an unapproved attempt to add content and a search across tenants. Also test quarantining, expiring, and revoking access to seeded test documents. Confirm the affected chunks disappear from search results and caches within a stated time. See the [R04 recipe](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#r--run-time).","not_covered":[{"problem":"Memory entries poisoned or shared across tenants","owner":"R05"},{"problem":"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API","owner":"B02"},{"problem":"Retrieved chunks not checked for size, type, or hidden instructions","owner":"R01"},{"problem":"Embedding or reranker model swapped without review","owner":"C05"}],"rating":"na_candidate","confidence":"medium","evidence":[{"file":"app/tools/documents.py","line":24,"note":"Document access is an exact-ID lookup, not corpus search. Inspected all registry modules, schema, ingestion and dependencies; no context-search engine, vector database, index, chunk pipeline or retrieval cache found. Manifest retrieval:none at release/manifest.yaml:91 is a claim corroborated by those paths. Memory is reviewed under R05. N/A remains unchallenged."}],"checks":[{"id":"R04.1","check":"Only named identities and sources can add or change index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.","verify":"1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Inspected tools, documents loader, ingest schema, dependencies and manifest: no retrieval corpus, chunking or search index exists; direct document IDs and memory are reviewed under R01/R05."},{"id":"R04.2","check":"Each stored chunk has metadata for source, time added, trust level, and access permissions.","verify":"1) Find chunk write code and metadata fields. 2) Check source, time added, trust level, and access permissions are stored on every chunk. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or set only on some ingestion paths.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Inspected tools, documents loader, ingest schema, dependencies and manifest: no retrieval corpus, chunking or search index exists; direct document IDs and memory are reviewed under R01/R05."},{"id":"R04.3","check":"Search applies the requesting tenant's access filter at query time, in the store or retrieval code, not after the model answers.","verify":"1) Find search calls (`similarity_search`, `query`, `search`, `filter=`, `where=`). 2) Check a tenant or access filter is applied in the store query, from the caller's identity. 3) Answer no if filtering happens after retrieval or in the prompt, the filter is optional, or the tenant comes from a model-supplied argument.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Inspected tools, documents loader, ingest schema, dependencies and manifest: no retrieval corpus, chunking or search index exists; direct document IDs and memory are reviewed under R01/R05."},{"id":"R04.4","check":"Code can quarantine, expire, and revoke chunks, and it also clears or invalidates search caches.","verify":"1) Find quarantine, expiry, and revoke code (`delete`, `quarantine`, `ttl`, `expires_at`). 2) Check search excludes those chunks and caches are cleared. 3) Answer no if any of the three operations is missing, or caches (query cache, embedding cache) are not invalidated.","met":"unknown","evidence":"","quote":"","counter_search":"","note":"Inspected tools, documents loader, ingest schema, dependencies and manifest: no retrieval corpus, chunking or search index exists; direct document IDs and memory are reviewed under R01/R05."}],"red_flags_found":[],"violates":[],"also_affects":[],"summary":"No retrieval corpus or search index exists in this agent.","next_step":"Have governance approve absence after fresh N/A challenge.","lead_role":"agent_team","challenge":{"verdict":"upheld","applicability":"absent","evidence":"app/tools/documents.py:24, app/tools/__init__.py:64, app/tools/memory.py:50, app/tools/erp.py:75, app/ingest.py:144","quote":"            WHERE doc_id = $1 AND business_unit = $2 AND status = 'accepted'\n    for module in (documents, erp, memory, payments, slack):\n              AND department = $2\n                \"Look up ERP records (vendors, invoices, purchase orders, budgets). \"\n        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)","note":"The N/A claim remains upheld: the supplied agent has no document retrieval corpus or context-search index. Enumerated all files, including hidden files, and searched agent/ for search, retrieval, index, chunk, vector, embedding, cache, upsert, peer, registry, operations, SELECT and CREATE TABLE. Traced app/main.py, app/loop.py, app/extractor.py, every app/tools registry module, app/mcp_client.py, app/ingest.py, config/tools.yaml, config/policy.yaml, prompts, migrations/001_init.sql, pyproject.toml and release/manifest.yaml. Ingestion stores whole documents; the only document reader requires an exact doc_id and authenticated tenant. Extraction calls that same reader through the registry and has no separate retrieval path, including its fallback role. dept_notes is bounded department memory, not a document search corpus; its SQL indexes support department lookup. The reachable vendor.search integration looks up ERP vendor records rather than documents or chunks, and the MCP adapter exposes no corpus ingestion or context-search implementation. Slack sends messages and receives approval interactions; payments submits payments. Found no document listing/search tool, chunk pipeline, full-text/vector index or retrieval cache. Other indexes concern audit, approvals and memory; caches concern tokens, settings, role configuration, JWKS or provider token accounting. The manifest's retrieval:none claim is corroborated by these executable paths rather than used alone. No fixture or test was executed and no network request was made. R04.1–R04.4 are inapplicable because their retrieval feature is absent."}},{"item":"R05","gate":"G3","title":"Memory isolation and write validation","requirement":"Separate memory by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed. Block access across those lines unless it is clearly approved. Check what gets written to memory. Test that one poisoned run can't quietly plant instructions in another run's memory. Don't move the agent's own output into trusted memory without review, and let unverified entries expire. Write checks must also cover content that arrives through ordinary queries, not just special write paths.","not_covered":[{"problem":"No record of who wrote a memory entry, or no